# Delivery and operations

- **[FAST-CI]** The full CI runs in under 10 minutes; a flaky test is quarantined and fixed within
  the week, never re-run until it passes.
{%- if podman %}
- **[IMAGES-BY-DIGEST]** Every container base image is pinned by its `@sha256:` digest, never by
  a moving tag alone.
- **[HARDENED-CONTAINERS]** Rootless containers and a non-root user, a read-only file system
  outside declared volumes, `cap_drop: ALL`, no secret in the image nor in its layers.
{%- endif %}
{%- if server %}
- **[HEALTH-PROBES]** Each service exposes a liveness probe and a readiness probe; the second one
  really checks its dependencies (database, cache).
{%- endif %}
{%- if level >= 2 or deploy == 'vps' %}
- **[TESTED-BACKUPS]** A backup never restored does not exist: the restore is repeated at regular
  intervals and timed.
- **[REVERSIBLE-DEPLOYMENT]** Every deployment can be undone in one command, without data loss: a
  deployment that migrates the schema is undone by restoring the backup taken just before.
{%- endif %}
{%- if level >= 2 %}
- **[SBOM]** Each deployed image produces its bill of materials (CycloneDX or SPDX), kept with
  the release.
- **[ALERT-ON-SYMPTOMS]** Alerts fire on what users suffer (error rate, latency, a job queue that
  grows), not on internal causes (CPU, memory).
{%- endif %}
{%- if level >= 3 %}
- **[SLO]** Each critical journey has a service level objective in numbers (availability, p95
  latency) and an error budget. An exhausted budget freezes features in favour of reliability.
- **[OPENTELEMETRY]** OpenTelemetry distributed traces (W3C `traceparent` propagation) from the
  request to background jobs and third-party APIs
{%- if backend in ['django', 'fastapi'] %}; the `X-Request-ID` ([CORRELATION]) is their
  correlation attribute{% endif %}.
- **[FEATURE-FLAGS]** A risky feature ships off behind a flag, then turns on without a
  redeployment. A flag has a removal date; past it, it goes.
{%- endif %}
